	(text "IR transmitter: two 940 nm LEDs from VBAT, each with a constant-current sink.\nBase node clamped at ~1.3 V by two 1N4148 in series, so I_LED = (1.3 - Vbe) / R_E.\nVbe of a BC817-40 is ~0.75-0.8 V at 150 mA, leaving ~0.5 V across R_E: 3.3 ohm\ngives ~150-165 mA (4.3 ohm would give only ~110-120 mA), roughly constant from VBAT 3.3 to 4.2 V.\nSET R_E FROM THE BREADBOARD (scope across R_E at 3.3 and 4.2 V), and check the\nTSAL6200 peak rating for our duty cycle (39.7 kHz, ~50 % measured, in bursts)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 20.32 15.24 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "5974c1da-ed3c-536c-9279-8d8c1daf907f")
	)
